    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section provides an overview of the present study, outlining its three main goals. The study aims to investigate body-as-object versus body-as-process orientations, the relationship between exercise and body appreciation, and how weight loss and exercise talk predict body appreciation. It also hypothesizes mediation effects of body-as-object and body-as-process orientations on these relationships.",
      "evidence_source": "Overview of present study In the present study, we had three goals. First, we expected that women would endorse higher scores on the body-as-object orientation versus body-as-process, and that engagement in exercise would correspond to increases in body-asprocess orientation and body appreciation. Second, we expected that weight loss talk would negatively predict and exercise talk would positively predict body appreciation. Third, we hypothesized that viewing the bodyas-object would mediate the relationship between weight loss talk and body appreciation, and viewing the body-as-process would mediate the relationship between exercise talk and body appreciation.",
